{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788297628,"nonce":"nI3S03Lo1i/48dlGuVQGS6ioiAY=","title":"dev:add-gene — no shipped verb can make a pawn incapable of violence, so an acceptance fixture is a dice roll","message":"Found while building `accept/b1b3060-posture.py` phase 3, whose acceptance bullet\nis \"a pawn incapable of violence is refused BY NAME\". There is no deterministic\nway to produce that pawn from the shipped verb surface.\n\n## What was checked, against the game's own defs\n\n- **`dev:spawn-pawn {violence_capable:false}` does NOT do it.** The flag maps to\n  `PawnGenerationRequest.mustBeCapableOfViolence`, so `false` merely stops\n  *requiring* capability — the generator then rolls a backstory freely and the\n  pawn is usually violent.\n- **No vanilla TRAIT disables Violent.** The three trait defs that mention it\n  (`Data/Core/Defs/TraitDefs/Traits_Singular.xml` x2,\n  `Traits_Spectrum.xml`) list it under `requiredWorkTags`, which is the\n  opposite. `Verse/Pawn.CombinedDisabledWorkTags` reads\n  `story.DisabledWorkTagsBackstoryTraitsAndGenes`, `kindDef.disabledWorkTags`,\n  conceited royal titles, an Ideology role, hediff stages, quest parts and\n  mutants — and vanilla populates the Violent bit from only three of those.\n- **No vanilla HEDIFF disables it** — no `HediffStage.disabledWorkTags`\n  carries `Violent` anywhere in the shipped Defs.\n- **A backstory whose `workDisables` carries `Violent`** is the only route a\n  shipped verb reaches, and it is random.\n- **`PawnKindDef.disabledWorkTags`** carries it only on Anomaly entities\n  (`Data/Anomaly/Defs/PawnKinds/PawnKinds_Entities.xml`), which are not\n  colonists.\n- **Biotech's `ViolenceDisabled` gene** (`Data/Biotech/Defs/GeneDefs/\n  GeneDefs_Misc.xml`, `disabledWorkTags: Violent`) is deterministic and is the\n  obvious lever. **No verb can apply a gene.**\n\n`accept/b1b3060-posture.py` currently spawns colonists in batches of ten, up to\nforty, and SKIPS with exit 2 if none rolls nonviolent — which is honest but\nleaves an acceptance bullet unprovable on demand, and leaves up to forty stray\ncolonists on the bench when it does succeed.\n\n## Scope\n\nA `dev:add-gene` / `dev:remove-gene` verb, plural over pawns, in the `dev:*`\ntier — so the widget-gate rule does not apply and `Pawn_GeneTracker.AddGene`\ncan be called the way the debug action does. Provenance:\n`Verse/DebugActionsPawns` / the Genes debug menu. Read the write back:\n`GeneDefOf` lookups can fail on a bench without Biotech, and a gene added to a\npawn with no `genes` tracker is a silent no-op.\n\n`dev:*` is the right tier and `PawnFixtureVerbs.cs` is probably the right file.\nNot `dev:add-hediff`: a gene is not a hediff and the tracker is different.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `dev:add-gene {pawns, gene}` adds a gene and READS THE WRITE BACK, reporting\n  per pawn what took and what refused (no genes tracker; Biotech absent; unknown\n  defName; already present).\n- Refused BY NAME with the reason, never skipped — the shipped `Outcome` shape.\n- A bench without Biotech gets one clear refusal naming the DLC, not a throw.\n- `dev:remove-gene` is the inverse and is idempotent.\n- `accept/b1b3060-posture.py` phase 3 can then build its fixture in one call\n  instead of rolling for it, and the suite's precondition text is updated to say\n  so.","files":null}]}